# Chapter 11 requests. First create and apply the migration (see README.md), then: dotnet run
# (https://localhost:42111, Development). DevSeed.cs adds product 1 (Notebook, 1200 cents) on startup.
# Send the requests in order. Each "Expect" line is the status you should see.
# Signing in sets this host's cookie. VS Code REST Client keeps it for the next requests; if your
# client does not keep cookies, use the curl.exe commands in README.md instead.
# Order numbers are unique: change @orderNumber before you create the order again.

@host = https://localhost:42111
@orderNumber = AW-1001

###
# Sign in as owner-1. Expect 200
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-in/owner-1

###
# Antiforgery token for this user. Expect 200
# @name ownerToken
GET {{host}}/csrf

###
# Create an order for two of product 1. Expect 201 with "succeeded": true and the new orderId
# @name created
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{ownerToken.response.body.$.token}}

{ "orderNumber": "{{orderNumber}}", "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 } ] }

###
# Read it back. Expect 200 with unitPriceCents 1200, the stored product price
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{created.response.body.$.orderId}}

###
# The same order number again. Expect 400 "The order could not be created with that number."
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{ownerToken.response.body.$.token}}

{ "orderNumber": "{{orderNumber}}", "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 } ] }

###
# No lines. Expect 400 "Use 1-20 lines with quantities from 1 to 20."
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{ownerToken.response.body.$.token}}

{ "orderNumber": "AW-EMPTY", "items": [] }

###
# A quantity of zero. Expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{ownerToken.response.body.$.token}}

{ "orderNumber": "AW-ZERO", "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 0 } ] }

###
# Duplicate product lines. Expect 400 "Combine duplicate product lines."
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{ownerToken.response.body.$.token}}

{ "orderNumber": "AW-DUP", "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 }, { "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 } ] }

###
# An unknown product. Expect 400 "A selected product is unavailable."
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{ownerToken.response.body.$.token}}

{ "orderNumber": "AW-UNKNOWN", "items": [ { "productId": 99, "quantity": 1 } ] }

###
# Without the antiforgery token. Expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderNumber": "AW-NOTOKEN", "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 } ] }

###
# Sign in as owner-2. Expect 200
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-in/owner-2

###
# Another owner cannot load owner-1's order. Expect 404
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{created.response.body.$.orderId}}
